WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.009 --> 00:00:03.981
(slow electronic music)

00:00:03.981 --> 00:00:05.309
The university of Alberta has

00:00:05.309 --> 00:00:06.892
a lot going for it.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:09.560
It's pretty.

00:00:10.709 --> 00:00:13.661
Its bear collection is on point.

00:00:13.661 --> 00:00:17.589
(slow electronic music)

00:00:17.589 --> 00:00:22.172
And it's home to many an
eccentric and clever inventor.

00:00:23.661 --> 00:00:24.861
Are you human?

00:00:24.861 --> 00:00:29.501
Of course not, but that
shouldn't keep us from chatting.

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:32.229
Like this fella, Kory Mathewson,

00:00:32.229 --> 00:00:35.661
an AI researcher who
comes with a sidekick.

00:00:35.661 --> 00:00:38.994
(slow electronic music)

00:00:43.907 --> 00:00:46.548
Tell me about this guy a
little bit, or is this it?

00:00:46.548 --> 00:00:47.381
Sure.

00:00:47.381 --> 00:00:48.341
(both laugh)

00:00:48.341 --> 00:00:49.829
So this is Blueberry.

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:53.821
On Blueberry, I've
deployed the improv system.

00:00:53.821 --> 00:00:55.749
So there's an artificial
improv system running

00:00:55.749 --> 00:00:57.666
on Blueberry right now.

00:00:58.639 --> 00:01:00.181
Yes, that's right.

00:01:00.181 --> 00:01:03.264
Kory does improv comedy with a robot.

00:01:04.456 --> 00:01:06.064
I've been doing improv longer than

00:01:06.064 --> 00:01:07.129
I've been doing computing science.

00:01:07.129 --> 00:01:08.560
I've been doing it for 12 years

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.109
and I thought, you know, there's no more

00:01:10.109 --> 00:01:12.280
natural convergence than taking some

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.680
of these state of the art systems

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.901
and putting them up on stage.

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.409
One day, we'll make it to the moon

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:20.576
if this planet is not to be our last.

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:34.709
I keep thinking there's,
like, a ventriloquist

00:01:34.709 --> 00:01:37.445
or this is like a new age.

00:01:37.445 --> 00:01:39.138
That's a really good way to put it, yeah.

00:01:39.138 --> 00:01:40.378
With a strange twist on it.

00:01:40.378 --> 00:01:42.080
The piece that's different is that

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.308
I don't know what it will say.

00:01:44.308 --> 00:01:45.949
Anything that comes from the system,

00:01:45.949 --> 00:01:48.938
it's generating live in the moment.

00:01:48.938 --> 00:01:50.427
Blueberry I created you.

00:01:50.427 --> 00:01:52.680
I downloaded a voice into your brain

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:55.519
so that you could perform
in front of these people.

00:01:55.519 --> 00:01:58.469
So they do not know
what I am going to say?

00:01:58.469 --> 00:02:02.447
I don't know what you're
going to say either!

00:02:02.447 --> 00:02:03.858
To give Blueberry the power

00:02:03.858 --> 00:02:05.776
of surreal Canadian improv,

00:02:05.776 --> 00:02:08.038
Kory first had to create an AI

00:02:08.038 --> 00:02:10.288
that could bring the funny.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:15.815
Step one: he feeds Blueberry the dialogue

00:02:15.815 --> 00:02:20.065
from a bunch of movies,
102,000 movies to be exact.

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:26.055
All the movies, every movie for 100 years.

00:02:26.055 --> 00:02:28.293
And that's just so it can learn language,

00:02:28.293 --> 00:02:30.594
see how somebody responds
to somebody else.

00:02:30.594 --> 00:02:33.946
That's exactly right, it builds
kind of a language model.

00:02:33.946 --> 00:02:36.674
Step two: he trains Blueberry

00:02:36.674 --> 00:02:38.554
just like you'd train a dog.

00:02:38.554 --> 00:02:40.546
Rewarding it when it makes sense,

00:02:40.546 --> 00:02:45.055
and punishing it when
it spits out gibberish.

00:02:45.055 --> 00:02:49.226
Time to put this wannabe
Kid in the Hall to the test.

00:02:49.226 --> 00:02:50.059
Here we go.

00:02:50.059 --> 00:02:51.559
Start improvising.

00:02:54.125 --> 00:02:56.393
Okay campers, we're going to get ready

00:02:56.393 --> 00:02:58.546
for a real baseball game!

00:02:58.546 --> 00:03:00.946
Grab your gloves and
grab your baseball bats,

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:02.144
and let's get out there!

00:03:02.144 --> 00:03:04.227
Especially you, Franklin!

00:03:07.062 --> 00:03:11.645
Okay, okay. Well, why aren't
you ready for the match?

00:03:15.745 --> 00:03:19.073
Okay, come on Franklin, you
know how I feel about you,

00:03:19.073 --> 00:03:23.573
but you've gotta keep your
head in the game right now.

00:03:26.758 --> 00:03:27.956
He's threatening you!

00:03:27.956 --> 00:03:28.789
I know!

00:03:33.028 --> 00:03:37.778
Oh Jesus, put down the bat,
Franklin! What are you doing?

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:40.946
I've got nothing to hide. Look!

00:03:40.946 --> 00:03:42.346
This is all I am!

00:03:42.346 --> 00:03:44.766
Okay, we'll end it there.

00:03:44.766 --> 00:03:45.599
That's great!

00:03:45.599 --> 00:03:46.797
That's how it works.

00:03:46.797 --> 00:03:49.037
Obviously, some of the responses
are a little bit weird,

00:03:49.037 --> 00:03:50.048
but then it's really funny,

00:03:50.048 --> 00:03:51.856
because then as you're going along,

00:03:51.856 --> 00:03:54.146
it did hit a couple of things perfectly,

00:03:54.146 --> 00:03:58.098
and then it's like, it's extra hilarious,

00:03:58.098 --> 00:04:00.015
because now it's going.

00:04:01.898 --> 00:04:03.186
Blueberry may not be ready

00:04:03.186 --> 00:04:06.528
for its Second City audition just yet.

00:04:06.528 --> 00:04:10.778
But Kory has a higher
purpose: making AI relatable.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.366
Oh it's gonna move, it's gonna move.

00:04:14.366 --> 00:04:16.616
(laughter)

00:04:17.666 --> 00:04:20.583
There is a fear in society of AI.

00:04:21.488 --> 00:04:24.726
So, we are kind of humanizing this AI.

00:04:24.726 --> 00:04:26.258
We're taking it down a peg,

00:04:26.258 --> 00:04:28.256
we're saying don't be afraid of this tech,

00:04:28.256 --> 00:04:32.288
look at how cute it is, look
at how kind of naive it is.

00:04:32.288 --> 00:04:33.926
(laughter)

00:04:33.926 --> 00:04:35.904
You've done it again, Blueberry!

00:04:35.904 --> 00:04:37.106
Isn't there a flip side to that though?

00:04:37.106 --> 00:04:40.887
Then you make it cute and then
people start to accept it?

00:04:40.887 --> 00:04:43.568
You know, then we wake up and...?

00:04:43.568 --> 00:04:44.401
(laughter)

00:04:44.401 --> 00:04:47.578
I mean, I don't think that
will happen in my time.

00:04:47.578 --> 00:04:49.138
Hm.

00:04:49.138 --> 00:04:51.477
I'm sorry you had to hear that, Blueberry.

00:04:51.477 --> 00:04:54.786
When you're ready to turn
Kory into a human puppet,

00:04:54.786 --> 00:04:58.453
give me a ring, and
we'll bring the cameras.

